WEBVTT

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:15.190
Congratulations.

00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:17.210
<i>The Two Princes</i> was wonderful.

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:20.700
How do you feel about winning 
Japan's Best New Actor Award?

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:22.470
Your song was a huge hit, too.

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:24.540
You're breaking new ground.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.910
Congratulations on winning the special 
award at the National Commercial Festival.

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:39.220
Apparently, it was really popular there.

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:43.160
Your song has topped 
the charts three weeks in a row.

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:45.670
You've received an offer 
for another commercial, right?

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:54.440
Our next guest is STARISH.

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:02.900
STARISH's cross-unit project 
has been a huge success.

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:04.660
Thank you.

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:08.420
We're down to the final pairing of 
Hijirikawa Masato-kun and Ichinose Tokiya-kun.

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:12.910
Your members' past successes 
must put a lot of pressure on you.

00:01:12.910 --> 00:01:15.140
I feel no pressure.

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:18.010
If anything, I'm excited.

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:11.960
Thank you for waiting!

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:13.920
Mr. Hijirikawa!

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:15.880
Mr. Ichinose!

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:19.630
I've chosen your cross-unit job!

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:27.910
The final phase of the STARISH 
cross-unit project is...

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:34.900
Performing at the Neo Dream Music Festival!

00:03:36.130 --> 00:03:38.290
The Neo Dream Music Festival?

00:03:38.290 --> 00:03:39.550
Us?

00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:41.860
That's amazing!

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:49.440
Hosted by five TV stations, the Neo Dream Music Festival is a summer dream!

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:53.790
You will be representing STARISH.

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:59.090
With a dreamy song and a great performance, 
please do your best!

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:01.430
And good luck!

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:11.570
The two previous cross-unit songs 
were for a musical and commercial.

00:04:11.570 --> 00:04:14.160
But there are no restrictions this time.

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:18.960
That freedom makes it harder 
to come up with something.

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:19.690
Yes.

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:25.280
We're free to choose our own melody and lyrics, but I want it to be special.

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:30.040
I'd like to write a song 
for the men you are now.

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:31.730
For the men...

00:04:31.730 --> 00:04:33.760
We are now?

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:34.620
Yes.

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:39.340
A song that reflects how you feel now.

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:43.800
The lyrics...

00:04:46.690 --> 00:04:49.430
This time, let's try...

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:51.560
...writing the lyrics first.

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:55.140
That's a wonderful idea!

00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:59.940
You two are perfectly in sync 
on your regular travel show, too.

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:10.050
The last episode was wonderful.

00:05:14.920 --> 00:05:20.410
Since I started working on that show, 
I've realized we get along surprisingly well.

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:25.720
I get so caught up in our conversations, 
the times flies by.

00:05:26.070 --> 00:05:31.310
I look forward to seeing 
what lyrics you come up with together.

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:35.910
Saotome-san didn't allow us 
to enter the Triple S once.

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:39.900
But through our efforts, 
I feel like we're closer to achieving it.

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:41.040
Yes.

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:46.200
Whether or not it happens 
will depend on our song.

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:49.820
Revolution.

00:05:50.980 --> 00:05:52.110
Revolution.

00:05:54.110 --> 00:05:57.290
Revolution!

00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:02.000
Revolution...

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:07.100
Our song will be a total revolution.

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:10.120
I know we can do it.

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:10.720
Yes.

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:12.200
Hey!

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:13.930
Hey, Tokiya!

00:06:14.150 --> 00:06:15.350
Guys.

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:17.580
We heard from Ringo-chan.

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:20.940
It's amazing that you're performing 
at the Neo Dream Music Festival.

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:23.850
It's amazing, Masato and Tokiya.

00:06:25.330 --> 00:06:28.240
What is the Neo Dream Music Festival?

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:30.780
Oh, right. You don't know.

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:38.660
The Neo Dream Music Festival is an annual 
event where Japan's iconic singers perform.

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:41.210
They sing all new songs.

00:06:41.210 --> 00:06:43.530
It's all broadcast live, too.

00:06:43.530 --> 00:06:45.930
It gets high ratings ever year.

00:06:45.930 --> 00:06:49.090
It's a music program watched by everyone.

00:06:50.690 --> 00:06:52.340
That really is incredible.

00:06:52.630 --> 00:06:54.210
Yeah, it is.

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:58.070
We were just discussing the song.

00:06:58.070 --> 00:07:01.050
They said they'd like to write 
the lyrics first this time.

00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:02.770
Really?

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:04.610
I'm so excited.

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:08.540
Be careful you don't 
end up fighting like we did.

00:07:09.210 --> 00:07:12.010
Masato and Tokiya won't fight.

00:07:12.010 --> 00:07:13.680
Probably not.

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:16.910
Huh? Where's Natsuki?

00:07:17.190 --> 00:07:19.580
Masato-kun! Tokiya-kun!

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:23.380
I baked something to cheer you on!

00:07:25.690 --> 00:07:27.330
Don't, Natsuki!

00:07:27.330 --> 00:07:28.960
Not those!

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:31.220
What? Why not?

00:07:36.150 --> 00:07:37.780
These have bite.

00:07:38.250 --> 00:07:40.600
They're not for Icchi and Hijirikawa.

00:07:41.070 --> 00:07:43.560
They're good. Try some.

00:07:43.790 --> 00:07:45.210
No!

00:07:49.310 --> 00:07:50.570
Syo, hang in there!

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:55.140
Be quiet! We don't want to bother them!

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:05.830
They're so focused.

00:08:06.290 --> 00:08:07.480
No surprise there.

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:34.790
You can tell Tokki's really serious.

00:08:34.790 --> 00:08:36.950
They're writing the lyrics first this time.

00:08:37.470 --> 00:08:41.250
I know they'll write something 
unbelievably amazing.

00:09:10.010 --> 00:09:13.030
His handwriting's more powerful than ever.

00:09:13.730 --> 00:09:14.860
Yeah.

00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:21.330
I'm so excited to see what kind 
of wonderful song they'll make.

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:25.280
I'm excited, too, but what's that?

00:09:25.280 --> 00:09:28.030
New Piyo-chan merchandise.

00:09:28.030 --> 00:09:29.330
This is for you.

00:09:30.840 --> 00:09:32.470
Stop that!

00:09:31.330 --> 00:09:33.890
But it looks great on you.

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:36.170
Masato and Tokiya think and sing similarly.

00:09:36.440 --> 00:09:40.010
If all goes well, their synergy 
will produce something amazing.

00:09:40.910 --> 00:09:42.850
But one mistake, and...

00:09:43.120 --> 00:09:43.840
What?

00:09:45.050 --> 00:09:49.010
They could end up in a deadlock.

00:09:49.010 --> 00:09:51.410
That's not possible.

00:09:51.410 --> 00:09:52.650
Yeah.

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:05.870
Let me fly over the rainbow, yeah.

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:07.790
Go, now. Go...

00:10:08.130 --> 00:10:13.250
The time has come, heroes, 
to travel across the deep blue sea...

00:10:20.790 --> 00:10:22.560
Heart breaking.

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:25.360
Like a lonely bird who can't fly 
looking up at the stars.

00:10:25.360 --> 00:10:27.180
Always dreaming...

00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:30.250
This once-in-a-lifetime connection.

00:10:30.250 --> 00:10:32.650
I will never forget 
these overflowing feelings...

00:10:36.680 --> 00:10:38.390
Nothing feels quite right.

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:40.760
It's missing something.

00:10:40.760 --> 00:10:41.580
Yes.

00:10:42.690 --> 00:10:45.200
Perhaps we should organize our thoughts.

00:10:45.570 --> 00:10:48.910
Yes. We should change our thinking.

00:10:50.230 --> 00:10:54.070
Why don't we consider 
what we have in common?

00:10:54.070 --> 00:10:55.710
Good idea.

00:10:55.710 --> 00:11:00.500
Besides the travel program, 
together, we've worked on...

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:02.680
We weren't working together,

00:11:03.420 --> 00:11:08.700
but when I auditioned for the play, 
you helped me practice.

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:19.720
I learned from you then that I must 
be thorough in everything I do.

00:11:19.720 --> 00:11:20.740
Really?

00:11:21.850 --> 00:11:26.080
While practicing the dance for 
<i>Maji LOVE Revolution 2000%,</i>

00:11:27.210 --> 00:11:30.360
I was moved by your effort.

00:11:34.410 --> 00:11:35.480
I see.

00:11:35.480 --> 00:11:36.170
Yes.

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:48.060
It's difficult to change one's thinking.

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:52.520
If I could just think of something, 
I know I'd see the way.

00:11:52.810 --> 00:11:53.820
The way?

00:11:53.820 --> 00:11:54.660
Yes.

00:11:55.700 --> 00:12:00.170
Whenever my thoughts are lost in a maze, 
there's a place I always go.

00:12:00.170 --> 00:12:01.100
A place?

00:12:01.100 --> 00:12:01.860
Yes.

00:12:02.230 --> 00:12:03.910
Where?

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:05.450
A waterfall.

00:12:05.450 --> 00:12:06.210
A waterfall?

00:12:06.210 --> 00:12:07.620
Yes, a waterfall.

00:12:09.100 --> 00:12:10.740
A waterfall...

00:12:10.740 --> 00:12:12.860
When meditating under a waterfall,

00:12:12.860 --> 00:12:15.860
sometimes the way suddenly 
appears before you.

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:20.810
If you think it will work, 
let's go immediately!

00:12:34.580 --> 00:12:36.820
We couldn't see the way.

00:12:37.790 --> 00:12:40.200
All we saw was water.

00:12:50.470 --> 00:12:51.850
This handwriting...

00:12:51.850 --> 00:12:53.590
It's Nanami-san's handwriting.

00:12:53.590 --> 00:12:55.140
She did this for us.

00:12:55.140 --> 00:12:56.170
I am grateful.

00:12:56.170 --> 00:12:58.220
Let's do our best, Hijirikawa-san.

00:12:58.220 --> 00:12:58.920
Yes.

00:13:03.360 --> 00:13:06.090
What? They're still not finished?

00:13:06.330 --> 00:13:11.100
No. They're working hard.

00:13:11.460 --> 00:13:13.640
But they can't decide.

00:13:14.140 --> 00:13:19.060
It's not good that you don't have lyrics 
yet since you're writing those first.

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:22.070
Won't it affect your schedule?

00:13:22.070 --> 00:13:24.570
I'll be fine.

00:13:24.830 --> 00:13:26.120
Come on!

00:13:26.120 --> 00:13:28.570
Ma-kun, Tokiya-chan, you can do it!

00:13:31.800 --> 00:13:36.070
Because they're similar, 
it's possible they'll reach a deadlock.

00:13:36.070 --> 00:13:39.130
My concern became reality.

00:13:39.930 --> 00:13:42.570
They'll just have to tackle it head on.

00:13:43.430 --> 00:13:46.490
They've got talent.

00:13:46.490 --> 00:13:48.840
If they approached it normally, 
I know they could do it.

00:13:51.080 --> 00:13:55.140
If they can't even write lyrics, 
it means that's all they were.

00:13:56.200 --> 00:13:58.160
So it's their moment of truth.

00:13:58.730 --> 00:13:59.950
Let's see what they do.

00:14:02.140 --> 00:14:03.820
That's a huge concern!

00:14:04.100 --> 00:14:08.250
Isn't there anything we can do to help?

00:14:08.250 --> 00:14:09.410
It's okay.

00:14:10.580 --> 00:14:14.120
They're definitely 
come up with some good lyrics.

00:14:15.010 --> 00:14:16.280
You're right.

00:14:17.560 --> 00:14:18.370
Yeah, you're right.

00:14:18.720 --> 00:14:19.670
Yeah.

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:20.530
Yeah!

00:14:29.170 --> 00:14:34.050
So that's what's happening.

00:14:34.050 --> 00:14:34.870
Yes.

00:14:36.260 --> 00:14:37.730
Exciting.

00:14:37.970 --> 00:14:38.940
What?

00:14:39.190 --> 00:14:44.900
How they overcome this situation 
will show us their true worth!

00:14:51.090 --> 00:14:54.250
Why is this happening?

00:14:55.250 --> 00:14:58.410
I can't believe we don't know how 
to get out of this situation.

00:14:58.810 --> 00:15:01.830
Nanami needs time to compose a song.

00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:04.750
What should we do?

00:15:05.100 --> 00:15:08.340
We need to solve this ourselves.

00:15:09.350 --> 00:15:13.720
They say, "Heaven helps 
those who help themselves."

00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:26.090
Come to think of it, we haven't 
seen the others much lately.

00:15:26.090 --> 00:15:28.580
They must be busy with work.

00:15:28.580 --> 00:15:29.950
Probably.

00:15:30.200 --> 00:15:32.360
Hijirikawa-san, Ichinose-san.

00:15:37.810 --> 00:15:40.040
Um.. They're not.

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:47.230
They've been trying not to bother you, 
so you can focus on writing.

00:15:48.590 --> 00:15:50.170
We've been talking.

00:15:52.500 --> 00:15:57.730
Let's avoid the salon while 
they're meeting, so they can focus.

00:15:57.730 --> 00:15:59.590
Good idea, Shorty.

00:15:59.590 --> 00:16:00.850
Don't call me Shorty!

00:16:01.350 --> 00:16:06.840
I'm going to stay away from 
the dorms while they're writing.

00:16:06.840 --> 00:16:10.010
I see. That's a good idea.

00:16:10.330 --> 00:16:11.390
Yes!

00:16:11.390 --> 00:16:15.370
I'm going to focus on folding 
a thousand Piyo-chans!

00:16:15.600 --> 00:16:16.530
Good idea.

00:16:16.530 --> 00:16:17.990
I'll help.

00:16:17.990 --> 00:16:19.560
It'll be amazing.

00:16:20.300 --> 00:16:24.570
Everyone helped make 
the food in the basket.

00:16:24.570 --> 00:16:25.330
What?

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:27.390
But your note...

00:16:27.810 --> 00:16:29.050
They asked me to do it.

00:16:37.120 --> 00:16:39.080
Haru-chan, will you write the note?

00:16:39.080 --> 00:16:39.950
What?

00:16:39.950 --> 00:16:43.690
It'll distract them if they think it's from us.

00:16:44.690 --> 00:16:47.580
There's no point in making 
someone worry with a gift.

00:16:55.070 --> 00:16:58.390
They've been supporting us.

00:16:58.390 --> 00:17:03.150
We were so caught up in writing, 
we didn't realize what they were doing for us.

00:17:04.320 --> 00:17:05.850
This isn't good.

00:17:05.850 --> 00:17:08.880
I said I didn't feel any pressure.

00:17:09.120 --> 00:17:11.500
But we were actually feeling it quite a lot.

00:17:12.040 --> 00:17:12.770
Yes.

00:17:17.330 --> 00:17:18.870
I am ashamed of myself.

00:17:18.870 --> 00:17:22.420
And I am touched by their kindness.

00:17:22.420 --> 00:17:25.470
We don't create music by ourselves.

00:17:25.470 --> 00:17:28.960
It takes shape through 
our connections to the others.

00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:44.610
What was that song?

00:17:45.650 --> 00:17:50.130
The melody popped into my head 
while I was watching you two.

00:17:50.450 --> 00:17:52.670
It's a beautiful melody.

00:17:52.670 --> 00:17:54.460
Will you play it again?

00:17:54.730 --> 00:17:55.670
Yes.

00:18:19.650 --> 00:18:20.820
That's wonderful!

00:18:22.690 --> 00:18:24.370
I have no doubts, anymore.

00:18:24.850 --> 00:18:26.750
Only we can produce this.

00:18:27.150 --> 00:18:28.870
There's nothing in the world like...

00:18:29.240 --> 00:18:30.580
This resonance.

00:19:05.210 --> 00:19:06.690
It's starting.

00:19:06.690 --> 00:19:10.740
Masato and Tokiya are broadcasting 
from the outdoor stage.

00:19:11.330 --> 00:19:12.690
We'll see what happens.

00:19:12.690 --> 00:19:14.290
Fight, boys!

00:19:17.970 --> 00:19:20.210
They're on pretty early, right?

00:19:20.210 --> 00:19:22.710
Yeah. They're next!

00:19:22.710 --> 00:19:23.560
What?

00:19:23.560 --> 00:19:25.120
You can do it, Tokiya!

00:19:27.580 --> 00:19:29.900
It's starting, Hijirikawa.

00:19:29.900 --> 00:19:34.570
Next is the first appearance 
of STARISH's cross-unit group!

00:19:34.570 --> 00:19:37.980
Here are Hijirikawa Masato-san 
and Ichinose Tokiya-san!

00:22:14.800 --> 00:22:18.020
Revolution!

00:24:06.520 --> 00:24:08.200
With great sincerity...

00:24:08.200 --> 00:24:09.940
And my overwhelming love for you.

00:24:09.940 --> 00:24:11.090
Uta Pri.
